p({
"class":"foam.core.reflow.Flow",
"name":"MCP:dao_find",
"category":"MCP",
"keywords":["mcp","dao","find"],
"script":"[{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# dao_find\\n\\nFind a single object by its primary key / ID.\\n\\n## Parameters\\n\\n- **dao** (required): DAO name (e.g. `userDAO`).\\n- **id** (required): The primary key value. For numeric IDs pass as a string (e.g. `\\\"49393173\\\"`). For string IDs pass the value directly (e.g. `\\\"MCP:dao_find\\\"`).\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Returns a 404-style error if the object is not found.\\n- Call `dao_getOf` to learn the type and name of the primary key property before calling this.\\n- For DAOs with non-standard primary keys (not `id`), use `dao_select` with a query instead.\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n```\\ndao_find(dao='userDAO', id='49393173')\\ndao_find(dao='flowDAO', id='MCP:dao_find')\\n```\"}}]",
"created":"2026-06-20T15:30:40.095Z",
"lastModified":"2026-06-20T15:30:40.095Z"
})
p({
"class":"foam.core.reflow.Flow",
"name":"MCP:dao_getOf",
"category":"MCP",
"keywords":["mcp","dao","schema","model"],
"script":"[{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# dao_getOf\\n\\nGet the model schema for a DAO's object type. Returns all properties with their names and types. Call this before querying or writing to an unfamiliar DAO.\\n\\n## Parameters\\n\\n- **dao** (required): DAO name (e.g. `userDAO`).\\n\\n## Response\\n\\nReturns a schema object:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\": \\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\n  \\\"properties\\\": [\\n    { \\\"name\\\": \\\"id\\\",          \\\"type\\\": \\\"long\\\" },\\n    { \\\"name\\\": \\\"email\\\",       \\\"type\\\": \\\"String\\\" },\\n    { \\\"name\\\": \\\"loginEnabled\\\",\\\"type\\\": \\\"boolean\\\", \\\"required\\\": true }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Common Types\\n\\n| Type | Notes |\\n|---|---|\\n| `String` | Text value |\\n| `long` / `int` | Integer numeric |\\n| `double` / `float` | Decimal numeric |\\n| `boolean` | `true` or `false` |\\n| `Date` / `DateTime` | ISO UTC string |\\n| `String[]` | Array of strings |\\n| Enum name (e.g. `LifecycleState`) | Use enum value name in AQL queries |\\n\\n## Discovering DAOs\\n\\nTo see all available DAOs:\\n```\\ndao_select(dao='cSpecDAO')\\n```\\nFilter to served DAOs only by checking `serve: true` in results.\"}}]",
"created":"2026-06-20T15:30:59.128Z",
"lastModified":"2026-06-20T15:30:59.128Z"
})
p({
"class":"foam.core.reflow.Flow",
"name":"MCP:dao_put",
"category":"MCP",
"keywords":["mcp","dao","put","create","update"],
"script":"[{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# dao_put\\n\\nCreate or update an object in a DAO. If the object's primary key already exists it is updated; otherwise a new record is created.\\n\\n## Parameters\\n\\n- **dao** (required): DAO name (e.g. `userDAO`).\\n- **object** (required): The object as JSON. Must include a `class` property matching the DAO's model type.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Call `dao_getOf` to get the model class name and required properties.\\n2. Construct the object JSON with at minimum `class` and any `required` fields.\\n3. For updates, include the primary key (`id`) of the existing record.\\n4. Call `dao_put` \u2014 returns the saved object (which may have server-generated fields like sequence numbers).\\n\\n## Example\\n\\nCreate a new record:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\": \\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\n  \\\"firstName\\\": \\\"Jane\\\",\\n  \\\"lastName\\\": \\\"Smith\\\",\\n  \\\"email\\\": \\\"jane.smith@example.com\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nUpdate an existing record (include id):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\": \\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": 49393173,\\n  \\\"firstName\\\": \\\"Kevin\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Authorization is enforced \u2014 you can only put objects your session has write permission for.\\n- Some DAOs are read-only or have restricted write access.\"}}]",
"created":"2026-06-20T15:30:46.918Z",
"lastModified":"2026-06-20T15:30:46.918Z"
})
p({
"class":"foam.core.reflow.Flow",
"name":"MCP:dao_remove",
"category":"MCP",
"keywords":["mcp","dao","remove","delete"],
"script":"[{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# dao_remove\\n\\nRemove an object from a DAO by its primary key / ID.\\n\\n## Parameters\\n\\n- **dao** (required): DAO name (e.g. `userDAO`).\\n- **id** (required): The primary key value of the object to remove.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Returns an error if the object is not found.\\n- Authorization is enforced \u2014 you can only remove objects your session has delete permission for.\\n- Some DAOs implement soft-delete via a `lifecycleState` property rather than physical removal. In those cases prefer setting `lifecycleState = DELETED` via `dao_put` instead.\\n- This operation is irreversible (unless the DAO has a journal that can be replayed).\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n```\\ndao_remove(dao='userDAO', id='99999999')\\n```\"}}]",
"created":"2026-06-20T15:30:51.608Z",
"lastModified":"2026-06-20T15:30:51.608Z"
})
p({
"class":"foam.core.reflow.Flow",
"name":"MCP:dao_select",
"category":"MCP",
"keywords":["mcp","dao","select","query","aql"],
"script":"[{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# dao_select\\n\\nQuery a DAO and return matching records. Results are automatically scoped to your session permissions.\\n\\n## Parameters\\n\\n- **dao** (required): DAO name (e.g. `userDAO`, `cSpecDAO`). Use `dao_select('cSpecDAO')` to discover all available DAOs.\\n- **query**: AQL query string (see AQL Syntax below). Omit to return all records.\\n- **skip**: Number of records to skip for pagination (default 0).\\n- **limit**: Max records to return (default 1000, max 10000).\\n- **orderBy**: Optional sort order as a FOAM Comparator JSON object (see Ordering below).\\n- **sink**: Optional FOAM Sink for server-side aggregation (see Sinks below).\\n\\n## Tips\\n\\n- Call `dao_getOf` first to learn a DAO's property names and types before querying.\\n- Only properties marked `searchable` on the model are available for AQL queries.\"}},{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# AQL Query Syntax\\n\\n## Logical Operators\\n\\nCombine expressions with AND (or spaces or `&`), OR (or `|`), and NOT:\\n```\\nfirstName = Kevin AND group = admin\\nstatus = ACTIVE | status = PENDING\\nNOT loginEnabled IS FALSE\\n(age > 18 OR group = admin) AND spid = paytic\\n```\\n\\n## String Expressions\\n\\n| Expression | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `prop = value` | Exact match |\\n| `prop != value` | Not equal |\\n| `prop CONTAINS value` or `prop : value` or `prop ~ value` | Contains |\\n| `prop IN (a,b,c)` | Matches any |\\n| `prop NOT IN (a,b,c)` | Matches none |\\n| `prop > value` | Greater than |\\n| `prop < value` | Less than |\\n| `prop >= value` | Greater than or equal |\\n| `prop <= value` | Less than or equal |\\n| `prop IS EMPTY` | Empty/null |\\n| `prop IS NOT EMPTY` | Not empty |\\n\\n## Number Expressions\\n\\n| Expression | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `prop = 42` | Equals |\\n| `prop != 42` | Not equal |\\n| `prop > 42` | Greater than |\\n| `prop >= 42` | Greater than or equal |\\n| `prop < 42` | Less than |\\n| `prop <= 42` | Less than or equal |\\n| `prop IN (1,2,3)` | Equals any (integers only) |\\n| `prop IN RANGE (1.0, 2.0)` | Within range inclusive (floats only) |\\n| `prop NOT IN RANGE (1.0, 2.0)` | Outside range (floats only) |\\n\\n## Boolean Expressions\\n\\n```\\nloginEnabled IS TRUE\\nloginEnabled IS FALSE\\n```\\n\\n## Date / DateTime Expressions\\n\\nDates in ISO UTC format. Supports partial dates (YYYY, YYYY-MM, YYYY-MM-DD, etc.)\\n\\n```\\ncreated = 2025-10-21\\ncreated > 2025-10-21\\ncreated IN RANGE (2025-01-01, 2025-12-31)\\ncreated NOT IN RANGE (2025-01-01T00:00, 2025-06-01T00:00)\\ncreated = TODAY\\ncreated = TODAY-7\\ncreated IS EMPTY\\n```\\n\\n## Enum Expressions\\n\\n```\\nlifecycleState = ACTIVE\\nlifecycleState != ACTIVE\\nlifecycleState IN (ACTIVE, REJECTED)\\nlifecycleState NOT IN (ACTIVE, REJECTED)\\n```\\n\\n## StringArray Expressions\\n\\n```\\nkeywords = mcp\\nkeywords HAS mcp\\nkeywords IN (mcp, dao, query)\\nkeywords NOT IN (mcp, dao)\\n```\"}},{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# Ordering\\n\\nThe optional `orderBy` parameter controls sort order. Uses the same `__Property__` descriptor format as Sinks.\\n\\n## Single field ascending\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"code\\\"}\\n```\\n\\n## Single field descending\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.order.Desc\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"code\\\"}}\\n```\\n\\n## Two fields\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.order.ThenBy\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"countryId\\\"},\\n  \\\"tail\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"code\\\"}\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Three fields, last one descending\\n\\n`ThenBy` is a binary combinator \u2014 nest it to chain more than two fields:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.order.ThenBy\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\":{\\n    \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.order.ThenBy\\\",\\n    \\\"head\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"countryId\\\"},\\n    \\\"tail\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"code\\\"}\\n  },\\n  \\\"tail\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.order.Desc\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.Region\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"isoCode\\\"}}\\n}\\n```\"}},{\"cmd\":\"markdown\",\"value\":{\"class\":\"foam.core.reflow.Markdown\",\"markdown\":\"# Sinks\\n\\nThe optional `sink` parameter performs server-side aggregation instead of returning raw records.\\n\\nProperties are referenced using a `__Property__` descriptor:\\n```json\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"<ModelFQN>\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"<propName>\\\"}\\n```\\nUse `dao_getOf` to discover the fully-qualified class name (`forClass_`) and property names for any DAO.\\n\\n## Count\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Count\\\"}\\n```\\nResult: `{\\\"value\\\":3}`\\n\\n## Min / Max / Sum / Average\\n\\n```json\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Min\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}}\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Max\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}}\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Sum\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}}\\n{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Average\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}}\\n```\\nResults: `{\\\"value\\\":1}`, `{\\\"value\\\":6}`, `{\\\"value\\\":21}`, `{\\\"value\\\":3.5}`\\n\\n## Projection\\n\\nReturn only selected columns to reduce bandwidth. Result rows are arrays: `[className, val1, val2, ...]`.\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Projection\\\",\\n  \\\"exprs\\\":[\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"},\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"amount\\\"},\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"mcc\\\"}\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\nResult: `{\\\"projectionWithClass\\\":[[\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",57869,99.99,\\\"5045\\\"],[\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",57870,120,\\\"6011\\\"]]}`\\n\\n## Sequence\\n\\nRun multiple sinks in a single call using `args`:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Sequence\\\",\\n  \\\"args\\\":[\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Count\\\"},\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Min\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}},\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Max\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}},\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Sum\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}},\\n    {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Average\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}}\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\nResult: `{\\\"args\\\":[{\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"value\\\":6},{\\\"value\\\":21},{\\\"value\\\":3.5}]}`\\n\\n## GroupBy\\n\\nGroup records by property value. Use `groupLimit:-1` for unlimited groups:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.GroupBy\\\",\\n  \\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"group\\\"},\\n  \\\"arg2\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Count\\\"},\\n  \\\"groupLimit\\\":-1\\n}\\n```\\nResult: `{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"admin\\\":{\\\"value\\\":2},\\\"paytic-anonymous\\\":{\\\"value\\\":1}}}`\\n\\n## Nested GroupBy\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.GroupBy\\\",\\n  \\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"spid\\\"},\\n  \\\"arg2\\\":{\\n    \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.GroupBy\\\",\\n    \\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"group\\\"},\\n    \\\"arg2\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Count\\\"},\\n    \\\"groupLimit\\\":-1\\n  },\\n  \\\"groupLimit\\\":-1\\n}\\n```\\nResult: `{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"foam\\\":{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"admin\\\":{\\\"value\\\":2},\\\"paytic-anonymous\\\":{\\\"value\\\":1}}}}}`\\n\\n## GroupBy + Sequence\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.GroupBy\\\",\\n  \\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"group\\\"},\\n  \\\"arg2\\\":{\\n    \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Sequence\\\",\\n    \\\"args\\\":[\\n      {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Count\\\"},\\n      {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Min\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}},\\n      {\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Max\\\",\\\"arg1\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"foam.core.auth.User\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"id\\\"}}\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"groupLimit\\\":-1\\n}\\n```\\nResult: `{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"admin\\\":{\\\"args\\\":[{\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"value\\\":2}]},\\\"paytic-anonymous\\\":{\\\"args\\\":[{\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"value\\\":3}]}}}`\\n\\n## GridBy\\n\\nA 2D cross-tabulation grouping by two properties. Produces both `rows` and `cols` GroupBy views simultaneously. Note the package is `foam.core.reflow`, not `foam.mlang.sink`.\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.core.reflow.GridBy\\\",\\n  \\\"xFunc\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"mcc\\\"},\\n  \\\"yFunc\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"__Property__\\\",\\\"forClass_\\\":\\\"com.paytic.atd.ATDTransaction\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"merchantCountry\\\"},\\n  \\\"acc\\\":{\\\"class\\\":\\\"foam.mlang.sink.Count\\\"}\\n}\\n```\\nResult contains `rows` (grouped by `yFunc` then `xFunc`) and `cols` (grouped by `xFunc`):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"rows\\\":{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"276\\\":{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"5045\\\":{\\\"value\\\":1}}},\\\"826\\\":{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"6011\\\":{\\\"value\\\":19}}}}},\\n  \\\"cols\\\":{\\\"groups\\\":{\\\"5045\\\":{\\\"value\\\":1},\\\"6011\\\":{\\\"value\\\":19}}}\\n}\\n```\"}}]",
"lastModified":"2026-06-21T18:36:12.107Z"
})
